So my next news article is about Homo naledi.

00:21:03.531 --> 00:21:09.654
And this is a hominid that was discovered not too long ago, 2013, in South Africa,

00:21:10.005 --> 00:21:11.666
in the Rising Star cave system.

00:21:12.286 --> 00:21:20.370
And it's been basically re-looked at because initially they had assumed its age was a bit

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.631
older and it has a smaller brain than us.

00:21:23.651 --> 00:21:29.934
So they assumed it was less intelligent and may have been walking around with our ancestor

00:21:29.974 --> 00:21:33.235
Homo erectus or the predecessor Homo erectus.

00:21:33.265 --> 00:21:36.867
But on a closer examination, they discovered a couple of new things.

00:21:37.647 --> 00:21:42.109
So they did six different dating techniques and discovered that it's actually younger,

00:21:42.529 --> 00:21:50.433
which would place it 335,000 to 236,000, which would put it right at the same time as Homo sapiens.

00:21:51.233 --> 00:21:51.653
Yeah.

00:21:51.673 --> 00:21:56.595
So this was another close relative living coexisting with us.

00:21:56.864 --> 00:21:59.245
So that's interesting in and of itself.

00:22:00.086 --> 00:22:05.068
But the really interesting thing that they discovered in my field is that they started

00:22:05.108 --> 00:22:10.251
to see evidence as they looked more closely at all the clues they were given that it was

00:22:10.351 --> 00:22:16.854
most likely more intelligent than we had given it credit for or assumed it to be, which happens

00:22:16.874 --> 00:22:17.675
with animals all the time.

00:22:17.724 --> 00:22:22.606
My go-to example always being alligators whose brains is as big as a thumb, but can learn

00:22:22.666 --> 00:22:25.507
schedules and training and their names and all that good stuff.

00:22:25.928 --> 00:22:28.189
That's basically what happened here is it had a smaller brain.

00:22:28.229 --> 00:22:33.431
So they assumed it was a little bit lower down on the intelligence scale.

00:22:33.831 --> 00:22:40.554
They assumed that it was also earlier and it was an earlier species that branched off

00:22:40.766 --> 00:22:46.269
before more modern, more big brain, more intelligent species came around.

00:22:46.489 --> 00:22:52.652
Led them to assume that it probably wasn't showing the more complex hominid behaviors

00:22:53.172 --> 00:22:53.852
that we start to see.

00:22:53.872 --> 00:22:54.693
If we do say so ourselves.

00:22:54.713 --> 00:22:54.913
Yes.

00:22:55.753 --> 00:23:02.276
The first thing that clued them into this was that where the fossil was found was in a cave

00:23:02.864 --> 00:23:08.586
and it was within one cubic meter or just a few cubic meters of sediments.

00:23:08.706 --> 00:23:09.667
Just a small area.

00:23:12.047 --> 00:23:14.829
Maybe 10 square feet is what we're talking about here ish.

00:23:15.569 --> 00:23:20.851
They found 1500 fossil specimens belonging to 15 individuals.

00:23:21.751 --> 00:23:27.653
That's a very high density in a small area, which points to that they may have been using

00:23:27.686 --> 00:23:35.690
this cave as a burial site to deposit dead members of their tribe, troop, whatever term

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:42.633
you would use for a hominid like this and doesn't show any signs of predation on the

00:23:42.653 --> 00:23:46.775
bones so it's not likely that this was a den where they were being dragged to and they

00:23:46.795 --> 00:23:48.536
didn't see any signs that it was washed in.

00:23:48.944 --> 00:23:54.446
So they were either going there to die or being brought there after death is what the

00:23:54.486 --> 00:23:55.667
clues point to at this point.

00:23:56.187 --> 00:24:01.009
And if that's the case, that's a higher activity that we don't typically see in the

00:24:01.429 --> 00:24:03.250
earlier and smaller brained hominids.

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:10.213
Which should be pointed out that that is a point that the researchers with Home on a

00:24:10.233 --> 00:24:12.174
Lady had been pointing out since the first discovery.

00:24:12.574 --> 00:24:12.914
Oh yes.

00:24:13.343 --> 00:24:16.884
They seem to be about the only people that think that that's true.

00:24:17.164 --> 00:24:23.928
There's a ton of other that's because and I think we said this recently about something

00:24:23.988 --> 00:24:26.529
else I think, that's a hard sell.

00:24:26.769 --> 00:24:33.912
And it's one of those things where it's hard to interpret, it's hard to interpret

00:24:33.952 --> 00:24:36.634
behavior from a corpse.

00:24:36.946 --> 00:24:41.588
It's really hard for us to, you know, it's one of those things where when we describe

00:24:42.189 --> 00:24:47.912
a velociraptor being the famous one with their large toe hooks, there is still discussion

00:24:47.952 --> 00:24:49.372
as to what we're using those for.

00:24:50.113 --> 00:24:54.415
We all have a mental image of what they're using for because we've all, any one civilized,

00:24:54.635 --> 00:24:55.755
have seen Jurassic Park.

00:24:56.636 --> 00:24:57.256
Yeah, absolutely.

00:24:57.276 --> 00:24:58.597
We're all on the same page.

00:24:58.802 --> 00:25:02.164
So we all have a mental image, but we don't actually know that's how they were using it.

00:25:02.664 --> 00:25:03.064
Same thing.

00:25:03.084 --> 00:25:03.384
Not yet.

00:25:03.784 --> 00:25:09.527
That's even more complex when you don't have a biological structure to infer behavior from.

00:25:10.388 --> 00:25:10.748
Yeah.

00:25:10.888 --> 00:25:12.589
They didn't have grave digging hands.

00:25:12.949 --> 00:25:16.731
They just seemed to have a mass burial.

00:25:17.331 --> 00:25:17.611
Yeah.

00:25:17.991 --> 00:25:21.653
The other thing that they pointed to with that, though, is that it is much farther back

00:25:21.853 --> 00:25:22.653
into the cave.

00:25:23.644 --> 00:25:29.368
If they were making their way back there on purpose, then they would be going into a perpetual

00:25:29.388 --> 00:25:34.290
dark environment, which once again to them suggests that they would be potentially using

00:25:34.370 --> 00:25:35.311
fire to go back.

00:25:35.931 --> 00:25:36.532
Interesting.

00:25:36.992 --> 00:25:43.075
The cool thing that they point out is that evidence of fire from, what was it, 1.1 million

00:25:43.104 --> 00:25:49.047
years ago, was found near that site just half a mile away.

00:25:49.167 --> 00:25:49.407
Cool.

00:25:49.607 --> 00:25:51.888
But it was assumed it was from our ancestors.

00:25:52.348 --> 00:25:52.588
Yeah.

00:25:53.008 --> 00:26:00.112
So if the clues that they're finding from those other findings is true, then this actually

00:26:00.152 --> 00:26:01.032
could have been from...

00:26:01.832 --> 00:26:05.254
We have now a separate possible answer, really, is what this is saying.

00:26:05.624 --> 00:26:11.507
There's also tools that have been discovered in the area that had yet to have owners placed

