And now these days it's, "All right, well, we weren't alone, and there were other...

00:27:42.065 --> 00:27:47.107
Like the Neanderthals, which were also quite advanced, quite intelligent,

00:27:47.307 --> 00:27:49.828
and Homo erectus was already using tools and such."

00:27:50.748 --> 00:27:55.670
And this notion of, "All right, well, so our ancestors developed high cognition,

00:27:55.730 --> 00:27:58.311
and we inherited it along with some of our sister species.

00:27:58.711 --> 00:28:03.213
But if Homo naledi was also doing potential tool use,

00:28:03.914 --> 00:28:06.194
and maybe even some of these more complex behaviors,

00:28:07.045 --> 00:28:14.508
that's... there was a potentially a diversity of fairly intelligent hominins,

00:28:14.608 --> 00:28:17.790
you know, human relatives, all living at the same time.

00:28:18.390 --> 00:28:20.731
And one of the things that this makes really difficult is,

00:28:21.332 --> 00:28:23.573
for a long, long time, we've always kind of been saying,

00:28:23.593 --> 00:28:26.554
"Oh, hey, we found tools, evidence of our lineage."

00:28:27.514 --> 00:28:28.635
