01:16:03.910 --> 01:16:09.912
And they compared basically the analogy they used was bacteria in a petri dish.

01:16:10.773 --> 01:16:16.135
And if you have a handful of bacterial cells in a petri dish and you chart their growth, right,

01:16:16.206 --> 01:16:19.007
one cell becomes two, becomes four, becomes eight, becomes 16.

01:16:19.308 --> 01:16:25.310
And the numbers will slowly increase, but it's exponential.

01:16:25.370 --> 01:16:29.112
So you'll get a slow gradual increase and then faster and faster and faster and faster

01:16:29.132 --> 01:16:31.213
until suddenly it jumps, right?

01:16:31.353 --> 01:16:33.193
A spike in population growth.

01:16:33.974 --> 01:16:38.276
